  "answer": "A \"Copy as Plain Text\" feature has been requested before. PowerToys#25192 asks for the same thing under almost the same title, and PowerToys#21001 asks for copying without formatting. #21001 was closed as a duplicate of the original Paste as Plain Text request, PowerToys#1684. Neither ticket has a fix. In #25192 the team said that when people want plain text, they usually want it either as \"as needed output\" or as an \"always\" option. Some users there said they would like a Ctrl+Shift+C style shortcut. Your case is a little different. LibreOffice Writer applies its own plain-text styling to text pasted by Paste as Plain Text. That detail isn't covered in the earlier tickets, so add it to #25192. For now, use LibreOffice's own Paste Special > Unformatted Text. Another option is to paste into Notepad and copy from there."
 },
